## Findings

1. blocking — brief:104 — The Health rows look like static text in the empty captures and populated 390 bottom capture: neither shows an expansion marker. The prototype’s `summary { display: grid }` removes the native marker, leaving both detail and the pause brake visually undiscoverable — replace with: “Keep both Health summaries at 13px/400 with a visible disclosure indicator that changes when opened; preserve keyboard activation and expose the pause/resume control inside Process health.” — check: `apps/web/src/components/w025.css`; `apps/web/tests-serve/w408.spec.ts` b5, closed/open captures at 1280, 640 and 390.
2. advisory — brief:17 — The captures show Needs you 4 and The Patron 1 without explaining their different units. Carrying the recorded spec advisory into screen copy would prevent these from looking like contradictory totals — replace with: “Identify Needs you as requests in Inbox and Work in flight as active work items from Board. Explain briefly that The Patron counts work awaiting a human gate; these counts need not match.” — check: `apps/web/src/screens/Officina.tsx`; b2/b3 captures with unequal counts and with an empty Inbox alongside a populated Patron group.
3. advisory — brief:96 — The agent-written requirement that every work row contain exactly two fields overextends the Patron’s removal of repeated state words. “The Patron / W-408 / Opening ledger” names the work but gives no clue which decision it needs; a distinct gate name would earn its place — replace with: “Keep the non-wrapping id and left-aligned title; omit state words that repeat the group heading. Permit a concise, non-redundant gate or next-action label when supplied by the existing Board record.” — check: `apps/web/tests-serve/w408.spec.ts` b3; replace the exact span-count constraint with checks for readable content and absence of redundant state text.

## Recommendation

The approved order, stacked groups and ruled rows make a coherent ledger at 1280, 640 and 390; populated views require scrolling to complete the burn and health picture.
The disclosure affordance needs a bounded correction, without redesigning the page or reopening the Patron’s rulings.
Beyond the overstrict two-field requirement, I found no additional layout, colour or initial-state choice requiring a new Patron decision outside the named Defaults.
W-202’s later modules remain appropriately outside this first cut; retain W-407’s predecessor relationship, the recorded scrollbar fix and build guidance, and W-406/W-415 behavior.
Verdict: revise